# KnucklsOS package list (Debian live-build: *.list.chroot)
# Debian base + KDE Plasma (Win11-style desktop)
# NOTE: the kernel is installed by live-build itself via --linux-packages
# (set in build.sh), NOT listed here (listing it causes a double-arch name).
kde-plasma-desktop
sddm
plasma-nm
plasma-pa
dolphin
konsole
kdeconnect
breeze
breeze-gtk-theme
papirus-icon-theme
fonts-noto-core
fonts-liberation
# Browser: Google Chrome fetched as a real .deb by hook 0500
# Gaming stack (all available on Debian)
# NOTE: steam-installer + its 32-bit deps are installed by hook
# 1000-i386-gaming.chroot (steam-installer depends on steam-libs-i386, which
# needs the i386 arch enabled first — that happens in the hook).
lutris
wine
wine64
gamemode
mangohud
vulkan-tools
mesa-vulkan-drivers
mesa-utils
# --- CPU + GPU hardware support (Intel i5 / AMD graphics) ---
intel-microcode
amd64-microcode
libgl1-mesa-dri
mesa-va-drivers
libvulkan1
# Firmware: REQUIRED for Intel iGPU (i915) and AMD GPU to initialize the
# display. Without firmware-misc-nonfree the kernel can't bring up the
# framebuffer -> black screen on real hardware (laptops/desktops).
firmware-linux
firmware-linux-nonfree
firmware-misc-nonfree
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-sof-signed
firmware-realtek
intel-media-va-driver
xserver-xorg-video-intel
# --- NVIDIA: NOT installed in the live image on purpose ---
# nvidia-driver's module/hooks fight virtual GPUs (Proxmox/VirtualBox/QEMU) and
# can black-screen the live boot. Real NVIDIA hardware gets it automatically on
# first boot via gpu-detect.sh (pkexec apt-get install -y nvidia-driver), so
# users with an NVIDIA card are still covered after install.
# Disk installer (Calamares — Debian's supported, themeable installer)
calamares
calamares-settings-debian
# GPU auto-detect deps
pciutils
polkit-kde-agent-1
# Boot splash + first-boot
plymouth-themes
# Extras
flatpak
gnome-software-plugin-flatpak
unzip
curl
wget
ca-certificates
